INSERT INTO `everlake_forge_stage` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(8152, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'These are dark tidings, indeed.$B$BNot a pretty sight for you to see, I\'m sure of it. Good of you to seek the proper identification for the soul\'s end.', 0),
(78089, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Katherine the Pure examines the orb with a worried expression.>', 0),
(78090, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So the Church of the Holy Light requires my aid? It will not come cheaply.', 0),
(78830, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Now there\'s a feather for your cap! Nicely done, $N.$B$BYou can rest here for a while, if you like. I\'m sure your trek through the desert was arduous.', 0),
(79229, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, so you found another one...', 0),
(79358, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A cleansin\' ritual usin\' the very twisted totems of our enemies? I knew tae expect great things from ye.$B$BLet\'s get to work.', 0),
(80411, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Some fine thievery indeed, $N. Now, time for step two.', 0),
(80526, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Alright then, let\'s get down to business.', 0),
(82084, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Your spellbook is ready, $N. May you fill its pages with arcane secrets to rival the ancient libraries of Elun\'dris and Zuldazar.', 0),
(82208, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thanks to your donations, the library is thriving.$B$BPlease, take this.', 0),
(83934, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hey! That\'s great! $B$BIf you find anymore of our coin, come see me. We\'ve got a great selection of goods and we\'d be happy to barter!', 0),
(84377, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Warchief of the Dark Horde is dead at last...$B$BThis is the end of an era of terror in our lands. And, perhaps, a boon in our efforts against the Horde as well.$B$BWe must let all of Stormwind know of your victory!', 0),
(86577, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, these samples are... gooey.$B$BSee how they are covered in tumors and pustules? These animals were suffering excruciating pain. Doubtless that drives their aggression.$B$BBut I do not know how to cure it. I suspect the solution lies on Hyjal, and we simply suffer the aftereffects.', 0),
(86585, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You found Ylva\'s body? Ah, the poor woman. She said she was going to show the troggs that Ironforge would never fall to their kind. She went looking for a few mountaineers who never returned from a patrol through trogg country. She was always too independent-minded to be cautious. Now we know what happened.$B$BI\'ll take the banner back and make sure it\'s cleaned up and displayed. You should take her weapon. May it serve you well against the troggs.', 0),
(86615, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You found it! Let me just make sure that everything is here... you can never be too careful with diplomacy!$B$BIt looks like nothing was misplaced. That could\'ve been a major diplomatic incident! Thank you for your aid, <Class>.', 0),
(86616, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, excellent. I will nullify the power of these Vilebranch totems and release it back into the wild. This will free the elementals to assist us, and undercut the power of the trolls.$B$BJob well done, <Class>.', 0),
(86620, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ahh, this is a job well done. So many little ones who now have a chance at a better future. We\'ll give them a warm nest and plenty of food, and they\'ll make fine partners.$B$BWell done, <Class>.', 0),
(87295, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'These look perfect! They\'ll make a fine set of shields for the local soldiers.$B$BHere, you\'ve earned this.', 0),
(89001, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Nicely done, friend! I\'ll fix this place up right away. Kick up yer feet and take a load off!', 0),
(89013, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ha ha! We\'ll be drinking good tonight. First round\'s on the house!', 0),
(89228, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Perfect, these\'ll cook up nicely!', 0),
(90487, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah... you have come from afar.$B$BHyjal suffers under the fel taint that rains down from the summit. The wilds... are dangerous to mortals.$B$BBe careful, traveler. The mountain has never been safe for your kind... and the dangers are greater now.', 0),
(90647, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Tiala studies the enchanted wand as you relay what has occurred in your journey so far.>$B$BKetharas created this... to combat Ve\'han Talongrasp? This is incredibly fortuitous timing, $N. Ve\'han and his Blackthorn Pact forces have been wreaking havoc here at the peak as of late.$B$BI think I know just the way to test this magic.', 0),
(90750, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Chuckling softly, Daythor shakes his head slowly side to side.>$B$BIt appears even you can\'t prevent our friend here from fulfilling their purpose. Shame, really... but at least they seem happy.', 0),
(90865, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Many thanks, $N. With their lookouts removed, it\'s only a matter of time before the remaining scourge presence is no more.', 0),
(91488, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you, friend. It will be good to sleep with a cover over my head again. And for you as well, if you wish.', 0),
(91531, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you, $N. Thank you from the bottom of my proud orcish heart! $B$BI would give you a kingdom if it were in my power! But perhaps you will settle for this.$B$B<Belgrom looks down into the sack with a hateful laugh.>$B$BYou should never have betrayed Belgrom, puny elf!', 0),
(91547, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Zevrost\'s eyes go wide upon seeing the tome. He looks around quickly.>$B$BDoes anyone else know you have this?', 0),
(91568, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hey, not bad at all, kid! Even if no one\'s in the market for these as artifacts, the metal\'s still good to be melted down and sold.$B$BGlad to see the Treasure Trowel\'s still in one piece too. I was worried it might blow up on ya!', 0),
(91569, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent! By this time next week, I\'ll be rollin\' in gold.$B$BNow, here\'s the plan...', 0),
(91608, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ha ha! Fetch us a barrel, $N. We will drink well tonight.', 0),
(91685, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So, no big score huh? Just a big angry dragon? Tough break.$B$BAh, what\'s this?$B$B<Izvi takes the Tear of Mennar, inspecting it with an eyeglass.>$B$BHmm. I\'ve never seen something like this before, but I know a guy who might. Good kid, works with the Bilgewater crew. He\'ll know what it\'s worth, if anything. Can\'t reach him \'til we\'re back in Orgrimmar, though.$B$BSorry to make you stick out your neck for nothin\'. Why don\'t you take something off the wagon? I\'ll write it off in the books.', 0),
(91688, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yeah, we know about the survivors in the village.$B$BFandral gave us specific instructions not to interact with them.$B$BNo, I don\'t know why. Fandral says a lot of things that I don\'t agree with. Not that I always follow rules... sometimes I\'ve dropped off a little food just outside the village when nobody\'s looking.$B$BBut he won\'t let us help them off the mountain. Doesn\'t want them \"interfering\" with things up here. I guess he has other plans.', 0),
(91733, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You look a bit damp, $N. Sorry about that. But thank you for retrieving the supplies.', 0),
(91734, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, so you\'ve been in contact with Andron have you? Well then, let us get straight to business.', 0),
(91735, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, so you\'ve been in contact with Jes\'rimon have you? Well then, let us get straight to business.', 0),
(91737, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, so you\'ve been in contact with Magatha have you? Well then, let us get straight to business.', 0),
(91754, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh, thank you! I will start mixing this into some poultices right away so that Fraxinus can feel better.', 0),
(91755, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Lovely! With these I can create some medicines for Fraxinus that will help to draw out the toxins that are poisoning him.', 0),
(91770, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Mmm... hrm... that feels... soothing.$B$BMy roots and branches are weak, but for a little while, at least, they are without pain.$B$BPerhaps instead of \"stranger,\" I might call you \"friend\"?', 0),
(91777, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh, $N! Thank you so much for saving my library. You\'ve done me an amazing service. Please take one of these fine weapons. They were intended for the militia, but you can make better use of them.', 0),
(91794, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hah, wonderful. Dese symbols of da Horde be a great way to keep everyone motivated, and to show da Alliance dat dey better remember who\'s on top!', 0),
(91881, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I am surprised to see that someone made it through the dangers of the mountain to reach Elderwild.$B$BWe haven\'t seen an outsider in... I don\'t know how long. You are welcome to shelter in the safety of our walls.', 0),
(91883, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you for returning my spear. I am glad to have a better means to defend myself from the Wormwings.$B$BThrough it I am able to better channel my spells, so I had felt like a piece of myself was missing in its absence.$B$BIt is a relief to have this spear safely back in my hands.$B$BThank you, <Class>.', 0),
(91923, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'With that monstrous hedge trimmed, the undergrowth here will be less of a danger.$B$BHyjal will bloom again.', 0),
(91952, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Greta is correct. The destruction of Archimonde at the end of the war rained down fel tainted ash all across the mountain. While I have been working to rehabilitate the landscape, progress is slow. Nature will eventually reassert itself, but the process may take many years.$B$BStill, it is good to know that there are still other people who care.', 0),
(92011, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You pulled off way more than I expected! That looks great! Who needs mining and blacksmithing when you\'ve got perfectly good hands to simply TAKE things with!$B$BWhile you were gone, I nearly finished up the battery cells and made some upgrades to enable me to control the Glaive Thrower from this console. Talk about power shifting!', 0),
(92014, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ha! That\'s the last time they\'ll steal my lunch!$B$BHey, for doing me a favor, I can give you one of these wards while we take a break. Care for a spring water?', 0),
(92016, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'If there\'s rootshimmer that deep within the waters, it shows the bottom of Nordrassil drinks deeply from still-pure sources.$B$BWe have time to put a stop to the Blackthorne rituals and demonic magic twisting nature itself, to ensure a healthy canopy for future generations. Thank you for assisting us, $N.', 0),
(92017, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This is a noble gesture, $N. Your own reverence, will, and purpose is already bound to these items, joining the spirit of the animal. With the wisdom of the wind bound within, this will aid our incense in stilling the airs from fright and horror.', 0),
(92020, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A book of sketches and notes about... giant lizards in Un\'Goro Crater?$B$BHonestly, I don\'t know if anyone has time to read it right now, but the author has a good eye. The sketches in particular are useful and informative.$B$BThank you for delivering this. I\'ll make sure it\'s added to the libraries of druidic knowledge of the natural world.', 0),
(92069, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have proven yourself equal to any warrior of the Blackmaw. As promised, your weapon. Wield it well.', 0),
(92147, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'With these losses, the Wormwings will surely be think twice about their brazen attacks. It is my hope that someday they submit themselves to the judgement of Aviana and atone for their crimes. Until then, we will not suffer them to live.$B$BRemain vigilant, <Class>. They are likely to continue to be hostile, especially after we have returned their aggression.', 0),
(92169, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'While you were away, our scouts returning from patrol brought terrible news! They saw members of the Blackthorne Pact dragging another captive Wild God into the lair of Ve\'han Talongrasp.$B$BThe time for testing is over, $N.', 0),
(92171, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ketharas sent you? He left us abruptly and has isolated himself for years. Yet now he deigns to ask for aid from the druidic order?$B$BNo, I will not turn you away. The threat you face sounds grave, and the Druids of the Talon will do our duty to the mountain.', 0),
(92317, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, this is perfect. Thank you, $N. I am impressed you were able to meet with Marrosis. He can often be difficult to converse with. He is correct; this is exactly what we needed.$B$BOnce added to our spell, this Drop of Stolen Life should strengthen its ability to draw out stolen power by acting as a counterbalance to the essence of life we already have and the strange energies of the staff.', 0),
(92335, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent, this pinch of ash provides just the sympathetic connection to make this magic work. It troubles me to use demonic remains as an ingredient, but I can set that aside for the greater good it can provide.$B$BWell done, $N.', 0),
(92344, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Just holding these roots, I can sense them teeming with an ancient energy. I\'m sure my study of them will prove quite fruitful. You have my thanks, $N.', 0),
(92346, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You\'ve found a tunnel beneath the world tree? Alright, I\'m listening.', 0),
(92446, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Dat is a great prize dat you have brought, and it will go in a place of honor in our village. You have saved us from much hardship. Thank you, $N.', 0),
(92449, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'We\'ve lost many trying to hold our ground. Perhaps this is just enough to make headway in eliminating their presence once and for all.', 0),
(92500, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Jewel of the Horizon! With just a touch of its power, we should be able to bring down Aviana\'s blessing upon our work.', 0),
(92519, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'No broken bottles? Yes, you certainly are a better choice for this than Jorell\'s lackeys.$B$BWe\'ll be able to use these to manage the ills of our patients a while longer.$B$BSince you\'ve proved that you are a natural to field work, I understand injuries come with the territory. Have your choice of the supplies, at least you\'ll make use of them.', 0),
(92533, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There\'s a darkness about you while you bear these armaments. I will unburden you, and with the Earthmother\'s blessing, we may have a chance of reversing this wickedness.', 0),
(92591, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'At last, we have a real chance. A chance to catch our breath, to build, perhaps even... to escape.$B$BThank you. We owe you our continued survival.', 0),
(92592, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Dis is a glorious victory. Well done. Now we destroy dis amulet, and we have a chance to finally be rid of da Scourge.', 0),
(92593, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Still dripping with demon blood, I see. Well done.$B$BIf your scouting is any indication, we\'re going to need to strategically eliminate the demon presence if we wish to restore safe passage through to the summit.', 0),
(92609, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Dem do just fine.', 0),
(92612, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '\"Old friend\" he names me in this note? That\'s rich. Well, the old hermit wouldn\'t send you to me asking for help unless it was truly urgent. His stubborn pride wouldn\'t allow it.$B$B<Dendrite studies the glowing branch.>$B$BThis magic... it is druidic in nature to be sure, but this crystal is all wrong. It stinks of fel magic.', 0),
(92702, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Fenwick reaches out to grab the other end of the tree branch.>$B$BAerrrgh!$B$B<Fenwick struggles as his oversized gloves snag the jagged branch, forcibly removing the gloves from his hands as he swings the opposite direction.>$B$BSorry, that\'s not working, I think if I keep trying to grab on I\'ll only manage to pull myself out of my harness!', 0),
(92743, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Look at this! Look at it! What a crown! Befitting of a Khan... but to be worn by Warug. I am pleased.$B$BAre you ready to learn the Magram\'s newest weapon against our foes?', 0),
(92755, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Your kindness is strange, nearly unheard of in these lands.$B$BDisenchanting equipment is still a foreign concept to me, and I often feel as though I am not drawing the full potential from these old items. These essences you provided help recover some of my losses.$B$BThe Gelkis Clan, and especially our mystics, thank you.', 0),
(92814, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'These are a little tattered and I see some frayed stitching, but nonetheless great quality. Better than most of the torn, battered, bloodied equipment she gets handed to her daily.$B$BYou have my thanks.', 0),
(92817, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hm. I suppose I was not specific enough in my request. Maybe there is still some knowledge to be gained here by studying this.$B$BRegardless, you continue to provide assistance to the Gelkis, so I will inform the others of your help.', 0),
(92818, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'THESE ARE PERFECT. BETTER THAN MINE. I HATE THAT.$B$BMAGRAM THANK YOU NOW. YOU TEACH ME LATER.', 0),
(92842, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'In retrospect, coming here was probably a bad idea.', 0),
(92844, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Orgrul begins to count the bones, but begins to skip numbers as they gain a second digit and eventually loses count. He tries a second time, but glares your direction partway through when your expression contorts while observing.>$B$BBah. I will count them later. This looks like enough. You had best not be deceiving me.$B$BI will hold onto these.', 0),
(92846, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Bwahaha, I heard their cries from here!$B$BThe Gelkis ought to learn to slaughter their own kin who betray their heritage. Failing to do so puts the burden on us to clean up their mess, and I am not here to tidy up after an inferior clan.$B$BIf you see more, be sure to snuff out the lights in their eyes. Once a Gelkis, always a Gelkis.', 0),
(92847, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Only three? Hmmph, Warug is being stingy as always. Give me a moment while I create the staves.$B$BI will take one. The second will go to the Necrokhan that patrols along the chokepoint toward the elven ruins.$B$BThe third is yours. You are a part of this war, now more than ever.', 0),
(92859, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'All right, I\'ll mix this all up and you can give it a whirl!$B$BNow remember, this\'ll only work in Winterspring. And it\'s not perfect invisibility, so don\'t get too close!$B$BWhat, you thought I was gonna try it out? I gotta shop to run!$B$BIf it works, I\'ll add your name to the fine print! If not... well, I\'ll remember you fondly. Good luck!', 0),
(92873, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I can see a new fire burn brightly in your eyes, outsider. You have demonstrated your ability to create your own armaments, summon minions to do your bidding, and most importantly to assert your dominance when they refuse to follow your command.$B$BA shame you have no centaur blood in you. You would be well on your way to become the next Khan.', 0),
(92878, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Blaise lets out a gurgling laugh; the sound coming from his neck. He puts Namida\'s hoof into his bag before scribbling a new line beneath his first message to you.>$B$BServes her right!', 0),
(92894, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Orgrul listens to your explanation, unable to suppress a grin.>$B$BDo not fret, outsider, for this experiment was anything but a failure. We now know how weak and fragile the Gelkis\' form of necromancy is. They have a long way to go before they will match our might.$B$BThe fact that you were able to seize control of any of them speaks highly of you, too. Despite those wasted skeletons, you have demonstrated your impressive capabilities.$B$BI will take the staff for now. There is more work to do.', 0),
(92911, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Here it is, $N! Should work great. Go give it a try!$B$B...Me? No, I\'ll stay here. It\'s starting to feel like home, anyway.', 0),
(92960, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Fascinating specimens. The closer they are in proximity to one another, the louder they hum. It\'s as if they\'re attracted to each other. Probably dangerous to intermingle this with other magical objects or energies, but maybe we can do something with them by themselves.$B$BLet\'s have a closer look.', 0),
(93035, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You looked battered and beaten, but not broken. Your efforts have made a difference to those that have been put back to rest, but I am sure you have noticed the turmoil in the valley has only risen.$B$BI fear it won\'t be long before those same bones you buried are back on their feet.$B$BWe must press on.', 0),
(93041, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Uthek listened to your explanation with an expression of doubt, until you presented the material evidence.>$B$BI noticed our dwindling numbers, $N, but never would I have expected this! Necromancy... shamelessly wielded by those foul Magram. Now I learn that my clan is involved too?$B$B<Uthek spits, only narrowly away from your direction.>$B$BI will speak with the Khan. For now, you will prepare to return to the front lines.', 0),
(93122, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<You summarize your findings.>$B$BNot one, but TWO camps?$B$B<You clarify that one camp is unquestionably Magram, but the other looks to belong to the outcasts.>$B$BThis means that the Magram are likely in an active conflict. $N, I think this may be our opportunity.', 0),
(93129, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Hagiak peeks into several of the crates without a word at first.>$B$BOf all things to bring out to the front lines, I would have never expected... nevermind. Some of these crates have food in them, and that\'s what matters. We\'ve shortened the time they can survive here significantly.$B$BThe ultimate victory for our clan grows nearer.', 0),
(93188, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'An interesting development has unfolded within Magram Village during your brief absence. It was an act of war, carefully executed by an outsider fighting under the Gelkis banner.$B$BHad this taken place a few months prior, I would have demanded execution of you and all other outsiders ignorantly playing deception with our clans.$B$BBut this is no ordinary circumstance.$B$BThis is an opportunity. For you, for the Magram, for the war.', 0),
(93197, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So, all the latest news from the mountain! I\'ll get this into the post and out to the right people.$B$BIn the meantime, while you\'re here...', 0),
(93226, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Gorhak\'s eyes widen as you offer up the bundle of carved totems, but his brow furrows as his eyes flick back up toward you.>$B$BI am no fool, outsider. This donation is not without cause. You want something, either from me or from our clan. I do not know what.$B$B<With a single swipe of his hand, the quartermaster claims the bag as his own.>$B$BAnd today, I do not care what your ulterior motive might be.$B$BWelcome to Magram Village, outsider.', 0),
(93269, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, you\'ve returned with mail from abroad! I\'ll make sure this is distributed to the correct people. Thank you so much.$B$BWe\'ve all been so busy with problems up here that nobody has time for the mundane details!', 0),
(93394, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It is remarkable to see that the pylons\' power burns brightly once more. I am surprised I hadn\'t noticed before you arrived. I was beginning to think that this one would soon suffer the same fate, and we would be lost to time.$B$BThank you for tethering us back in full to Shen\'dralas. Try to meet some of our denizens. They may be wary of you, but that will pass.', 0),
(93406, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hey, you got all the missing mail!', 0),
(93407, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Now, with these seeds, we can grow a stronger defense for us.', 0),
(93464, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Draenethyst, you say? Yes, I may know a thing or two about that...', 0),
(93465, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent work! Now, allow me a moment to transcribe these notes into something you and those lovely little bog dwellers can understand.', 0),
(93585, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The human you came with is a fool. He assumes our separation from the Light is simply a matter of ignorance. In truth, we were torn away from it, violently. Those you see here are all who survived. I will not have the history of the draenei belittled by such a man.$B$BYou\'ve shown none of the priest\'s arrogance, so I see no reason to drive you out the same way. Respect this place, and you are welcome to stay.', 0),
(93617, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Enough! You have proven my kin and I are no match for your brutality.$B$BYou seek to return us to our meek lives and violent deaths? So be it. Even so, this is MY domain, and though you have shown you have no trouble harming my kin you are not welcome to openly prey on them. You would do best to leave this place, mortal.$B$BGo then, scurry back to your dark-feathered master. Tell her we will relent... for now.', 0),
(93663, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Magtoor opens the box, inspecting its contents.>$B$BIt is delivered late, but all is as it should be. Thank you, <Race>. Send my regards to Dar when next you see him.', 0),
(93678, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Magtoor begins poring over the notes.>$B$BThis is most enlightening. Although, this sphere of draenethyst these notes mention; I have never seen it myself. I imagine you couldn\'t find one in a place like this, anyhow. If our mere shards already do so much for us, I wonder what we could do with an object of much greater power. Perhaps in finding that sphere, we could also find salvation.$B$BThere is much to study and consider here. It may be some time until we speak again. Until then, I thank you deeply.', 0),
(93759, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Wonderful. Let us enjoy what nature has to offer.', 0),
(93773, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This is terrible. Why would a druid do this to a Wild God? $B$BAs for this \"Pact\"... I\'ve heard whispers of a group of apostate druids that broke away from the Circle. The Blackthorne Pact, they call themselves... but I\'d never have dreamed that they would be capable of something like this.$B$BThis is terrible. Just terrible.', 0),
(93787, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Smells of earth and root, yes? Not pleasant, but we do what we must to survive.$B$BThrowing this into a boiling cauldron with fish and wild grass makes the pains of hunger retreat like cowardly human dogs.', 0),
(93848, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I am relieved to know that the magic we created was effective. It seems that this \"oldstone\" had at least one more bit of useful magic inside of him. I will also consider Tiala\'s offer... perhaps. $B$BWe have done good work together, and I hope that you will not forget this lesson: the wilds are bounteous, and beautiful, and they are worth protecting.$B$BI give you one last gift, a memento of our time together.', 0),
(93952, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You bring hope to our tribe. The chance to be friends is clear. Thank you, with your help the trees can stay tall and strong.', 0),
(94003, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have done what I could not and restored my family honor. For this, I will bestow a gift that few on Zephras are worthy to receive. I will teach you the secrets of the Skybreaker Defense.$B$BAlso, you will need a shield to put what I have to teach you into practice. Please, take this one. I have little use for it now that the Skybreaker Bulwark has been returned to me.$B$BBanu\'Adoraah, friend.', 0),
(94004, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You brought da elixir!!$B$BT\'anks, <Race>. You come all this way to help Sos\'mol. No ogre ever done that before.$B$BSos\'mol will remember this. Pay you back someday. Me promise.', 0),
(94218, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh, oh!! The elixir!$B$BMy, oh my. I am so sorry to have lashed out at you like that. I\'ve been on edge ever since I was told that one of those goblins has supposedly put out a hit on me!$B$BSadly I cannot afford additional security, so the best I can do is chug one of these and hope for the best. Cheers!', 0),
(94222, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Dis my new hammer?$B$B<The peon seizes the weapon from your grasp before you have an opportunity to respond. He swings it wildly in your direction, narrowly avoiding cracking your skull.>$B$BYES! Me fight back now. Won\'t lose this one, no way.$B$BTake dis. No idea what it for, but it fell out of slime creature.', 0),
(94227, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Cluck? CLUCK CLUCK! BWOK!$B$B<The chicken glares menacingly toward Magus Tirth from afar, newly acquired blade in beak.>', 0),
(94231, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ohoho, I take it back. Look at this beautiful boomstick. I bet it\'ll knock a satyr\'s head clean off.$B$BThanks pal, now step aside or you\'re going to get caught in the crossfire.', 0),
(94233, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ahh, my practice lock has arrived.$B$BThe Syndicate here have been plotting to turn this place into a prison like it once was. I already know that at least one orc is currently being held here. Maybe more. I don\'t intend to be another, but I intend to be more prepared than the last time if they catch me off guard.', 0),
(94241, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh your timing is impeccable!$B$BCallahan! Your new shirt arrived. Hurry up and change so I can stop hearing about how itchy you are all the time.$B$BAnd for you, <Race>. Here is your payment. Before you wander off, you should take a look at my wares now that you can afford \'em!', 0),
(94243, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I--Hmm.$B$BI don\'t remember why I ordered this.$B$B<Ziz shrugs and tosses the quiver into a nearby pile of junk.>', 0),
(94256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Fantastic, my Frost Protection Potion--expediently delivered! Why, I just sent that letter out a mere few days ago.$B$BI cannot wait to try this out! You see, I have been working on an incredible device, which is capable of...$B$B<The gnome excitedly yammers on about a peculiar machine that not even a certified Gnomish Engineer could ever make sense of.>$B$B...and that is why sometimes you need to be EXTRA careful when working with Frost Oil as coolant! Anyway, this\'ll fix it up quick.', 0),
(94427, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You... you are a paladin? Please, do not hurt me. I-I know I\'m not supposed to be panhandling. I have no quarrel with you or your order. Leave me be, I beg you!', 0),
(94468, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'By Madoran\'s beard, yer spirit burns brighter than any torch I\'ve laid eyes on, $N--and that\'s somethin\' to be proud of.$B$BKeep walkin\' this path, and the elements\'ll bend to yer will. Our kin will come to ye for wisdom and guidance. So let me be the first to offer me hearty congratulations--and present ye with yer newest totem. Ye\'ve earned it, flameborn.', 0),
(94500, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well done, $N! With all three samples in hand, I\'ll brew ye a vial o\' water so pure it\'d make the mountains weep. It\'s the final piece for yer rite o\' passage. I\'m proud to call ye kin, $N. Ye\'ve done shaman proud, and I look forward to hearing yer tales in the future.', 0),
(94501, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ahh, water blessed by Hervdana herself, and gathered by your own hands? A gift indeed. $B$BThese vials shall birth your sapta, letting you glimpse the water spirits at Stendel\'s Pond, near Moonbrook. The last few drops of the water have an equally important purpose... waste not even a cork stopper dampened with sacred water.', 0),
(94502, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You place the bracers atop the shrine and then pour the remaining drops of Norric\'s potion into dry stone. You begin to incant the simple words Norric taught you and the droplets vaporize atop the stone within the bindings....', 0),
(94615, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I knew it! It\'s those dang coyotes!', 0),
(94733, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Goblin sent you? Me no like little goblin. He talk too much.$B$BBut me help Chub\'chob. He good friend.', 0),
(94734, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You make good work.$B$BBerry smell yum yum good.', 0),
(94737, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'He said that? About me? Eh, no matter.$B$BIt\'s time we focus on what\'s really important--keepin\' ol\' Snufflesnout happy, and by Snufflesnout, I mean Chub\'chob.', 0),
(94782, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How many Scourge you have ta kill on da way here? Never mind, we just don\'t see too many people out here. Da village been trapped in dis corner of da mountain for a long time.', 0),
(94792, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent, $N! You are quite a fast learner.', 0),
(94817, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You took your time arriving, $N. But you can be excused given your dedicated service to the Light. Please pay close attention to this lesson.', 0),
(94818, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Continue your service to the Light and you will become a great priest, $N. Maintain your vigilance and dedication!$B$BYou are ready for your next lesson in service.', 0),
(94832, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hmm... T Belle you say?$B$BThat name does sound familiar... Ah, yes. Thomas! Thomas Belle.', 0),
(94858, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you, $N. We can all rest together now.$B$BIf you don\'t mind, I\'d like to be alone for a while. I\'m sure there are other families waiting for an adventurer like you. Maybe you\'ll even get there on time next time.', 0),
(94863, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well done, $N! You\'re quite in tune with the beast.', 0),
(94890, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Not quite what I signed up for when we started this patrol, but it\'s good we got here when we did.', 0),
(94891, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'With how long you were gone, I was starting to worry I misjudged your talents. But it seems you were just the right tool for the job.$B$BAnd that Riftan. Still kicking around then, is he? I just knew you two would get along splendidly!', 0),
(94894, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Troubling news indeed, friend. But this changes little. We are already at war, and on a much grander scale than a single hamlet on the outskirts of Alliance territory. We don\'t have the resources to support a personal vendetta.$B$BMore homes than those of the Riverglades have been razed by the Horde threat. If Brant could just put his ego aside, he and his cavalry could do great things for the Alliance. I see now that is a lost cause.', 0),
(94925, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yes, these will do nicely. Let me package them up for you to deliver.', 0),
(94929, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This is from Biggs? I thought he was dead. Now I recognize that scent. You came from the swamp, didn\'t you?$B$BThis shipment came not a moment too soon. With our ties to the Alliance cut off, these are the only provisions we can rely on.$B$BI\'d ask you to send my regards, though I imagine the journey here was enough to warrant at least a full week\'s rest and a belly full of meat. Please feel free to stay. You are safe within our walls.', 0),
(94930, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Where did you say you found this? I\'m surprised you\'re still fully intact. Thanks, kid.$B$BY\'know. If you\'re in the habit of doin\' favors, I bet plenty of folk \'round here will have a use for ya. Why don\'tcha stick around for a bit?', 0),
(94965, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'If I was you I\'d watch yer step around here. You may have made a bit of a mess by defeating Chub\'chob\'s friend.', 0),
(94981, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Just what we needed.', 0),
(94982, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This is quite gruesome, $N. Our allies will be pleased by your actions.', 0),
(94983, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Your findings are unsettling. And these... these are quite mysterious... How strange...$B$B<Sergeant Riftan pauses a moment to stare at the mementos.>$B$BThese carry a dark undertone--some kind of energy. Do you feel that?', 0),
(94984, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'As I suspected, magic bindings and a shadow cipher. It may take weeks to understand the contents.$B$BNevertheless, your work has been of delightful help, $N. I shall start at once.', 0),
(94992, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thanks for savin\' my Biscuit! You\'re a real friend, $N.$B$BIt\'s bittersweet knowin\' she\'ll be all alone for awhile, but hopefully we\'ll find a few of her stable-mates before long.$B$BNext time you see ol\' Demar, let him know Wheeler\'s Grange is back in business!', 0),
(94997, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Riftan sent you? That old dog has been battling those damn cultists so long I worry his fatigue has begun to wear on his mind.$B$BAh, I\'ve started babbling again. Forgive me. His concerns may be founded.$B$BLet\'s see what you\'ve got.', 0),
(94998, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The intricate work on these is quite remarkable. It would be a shame if they went to waste.$B$BTell you what. If you\'ll allow me to take a closer look I may be able to fashion something of use. All I ask is you allow me to keep one for myself for further study.', 0),
(95026, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A true hunter, eh? You bringin\' da safety to us here.', 0),
(95027, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Great! I\'ll just soak these overnight and they\'ll make fine feathered fletching.', 0),
(95033, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Heh, ol\' Tan\'jani sent ya? Good for him.$B$BWe\'re always looking for an extra hand.', 0),
(95123, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Whizzbuzz lets out a surprised whistle.>$B$BWhew, these are huge! Can\'t wait to light these puppies up and send those pirates sky-high!', 0),
(95194, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Shaw sent you then? Good. I was wonderin\' if Renzik even got my message. Come on then, it\'s not safe to talk here.', 0),
(95218, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh, Daythor...$B$BThis is the part of endless battles you won\'t often hear about--the torment suffered by those that participated in these events, particularly those who have witnessed horrifying things and remain for their minds to wander... and wonder...$B$BHe\'s been this way for so long. Perhaps there is something we can do to help put his mind at ease, even if just for a moment.', 0),
(95248, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yeah, we know about the survivors in the village.$B$BFandral gave us specific instructions not to interact with them.$B$BNo, I don\'t know why. Fandral says a lot of things that I don\'t agree with. Not that I always follow rules... sometimes I\'ve dropped off a little food just outside the village when nobody\'s looking.$B$BBut he won\'t let us help them off the mountain. Doesn\'t want them \"interfering\" with things up here. I guess he has other plans.', 0),
(95261, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Argo throws a hand over his mouth in reaction to the smell.>$B$BUgh...great work skipper. Now <hic> put those away before I get sick again...', 0),
(95267, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What the...ya actually got it!? Ha ha ha! $B$B<Argo clumsily snatches the creature\'s head, and looks it in the eyes>$B$BWhoowee <hic>, what a beaut! Think I\'ll put \'er right on the <hic> stern! Drinks are on me tonight, pal!', 0),
(95295, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It\'s not every day we get a visitor from Powderfuse Port. That\'s no small trek!$B$BI\'m guessin\' if you came all the way out here on your own you ain\'t in much caravannin\' needs, eh? Who sent you, then? Friz?', 0),
(95296, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There\'s no way I\'m lettin\' you into my town without me checkin\' your cargo first.$B$B<The wharfmaster clears his throat deliberately as he maintains eye contact with you.>$B$BNo. Way.', 0),
(95317, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<The crow looks less enthused the longer you explain your findings about the experiments, to the point where she begins to look bored.>$B$BYou dirtwalkers use SO MANY words to describe things. To what end I wonder? A simple summary of their evil deeds is sufficient, yet they record them in such detail. You mortals are an enigma, always sticking your beak where it doesn\'t belong.$B$BWhat\'s important now is how we will stop them and I have an idea. I\'ll find a tall cliff to drop these notes off of later.', 0),
(95318, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'From the more than murderous look in your eye, and the blood on your clothing, I\'d say there are fewer of those Ashen Reign fools than before!$B$BGood.$B$BNow we\'ll see if you can handle something a bit more... substantial.', 0),
(95319, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Wow, uh, why do most of these look so... slimy? Did you have to yank them out of the grime or something?$B$BOh, you did? Well that explains things.$B$B<Felflick rummages through the crystals you\'ve brought looking more and more distressed until he comes across the crystal that has a more uniform color and glows slightly.>$B$BAh HA! Yes. This one. I can\'t believe you found one in pristine condition.$B$B<Felflick snickers gleefully.>$B$BThis one will do nicely...', 0),
(95320, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Listen, by the looks of it you aren\'t friends with these pathetic excuses for warlocks.$B$BYou want info? Well I want revenge, and my freedom obviously.$B$BLet\'s make a deal.$B$BYou help me get out, I give you information and it just so happens we dismantle their operations in the process. Pretty good offer, no?$B$B<Felflick gives you an oily grin.>$B$BSo, what do you say, mortal? Do you want to know the dark secrets of the Ashen Reign in exchange for some teeny, tiny favors?', 0),
(95378, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Felflick cackles gleefully.>$B$BYou did it! Ah, I could hear the screams from here. Those meddling mortals got what they deserved.$B$BWhat you ALL deserve.$B$B<Felflick\'s eyes narrow dangerously, the grin never leaving his face.>$B$BBut, there\'s time for that later. I have the next steps in mind already.', 0),
(95380, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good, good!$B$BHalf of the plan is complete! Though, you should roll in some grass first to get all that ooze off perhaps?$B$BNo?$B$BSuit yourself. At least you sort of blend in with the slimes now.', 0),
(95383, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hello beautiful! Friz sure delivers, doesn\'t she? And look at the quality of these.$B$BWhat? Hey don\'t look at me. I didn\'t tell you to spend all your gold breaking the law. Far as I\'m concerned, this shipment\'s been cleared by customs. Friz\'s money on the other hand... that might be a problem.', 0),
(95426, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Wonderful work, $N. Resupply will take some time--and that\'s if their caravans make it here safely.', 0),
(95472, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'He did WHAT? That little weasel!$B$B<Friz balls up the shirt and stamps it into the ground.>$B$BNew lesson, lackey! Never trust a promise, and make sure to collect cash on delivery.$B$BWell, here\'s your share of the profits. No. Please. It\'s all yours, I insist.', 0),
(95511, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent, $N. I can see in your eyes that you have made a choice.$B$BI am so happy to be able to provide you with one of our sabers. I must say the one you have picked seems fond of you already. I hope you will take good care of it, and it of you.$B$BMay you both go into the world with Elune\'s blessing.', 0),
(95568, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I appreciate your aid. Each seed contains a spark of new life. Though Archimonde\'s destruction rained corruption down on the mountain, it is possible for nature to recover.', 0),
(95569, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I will keep these eggs warm and hatch them. After they are nurtured and grown, I will release them into the wilds. Hopefully, the slow process of healing the mountain will afford them places in which to make new nests of their own.', 0),
(95613, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'These will do marvellously. I thank you again for your help, $N.', 0),
(95647, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I thought we were done for! Something upset the wildlife around here and our excavation team was overwhelmed. Thank you for helping us with those spiders.', 0),
(95766, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So, a dirtwalker, eh? And one of the ancients sent you to me? Of course they did!$B$B<The crow seems to hold herself a bit higher, looking as smug as possible for a bird.>$B$BIf the ancients have seen fit to send you to me then you have already proven you are worthy of aiding me on this portion of the mountain.$B$BI may be a being of great intellect and majesty, but even I could use a wing with all of the troubles here. Who knows, if you\'re useful enough I may just make you my underwing!', 0),
(95770, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Kin\'weelay listens intently as you describe what you have seen.>$B$BYou are sure you saw the naga coming and going from this cavern ruin? Though what could they be looking for?$B$BPerhaps it is connected to I\'lalai after all. If this is the case, this could be the discovery of the century, $N! The Lost City has been a place of myth and legend for as long as any troll can remember.$B$BBut now it is possible the myth could be reality. There is no time to waste; we must investigate.', 0),
(95773, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good work. You are quickly proving your worth to the Horde with your work here, <Class>.$B$BPlanting these tridents outside the gates of Grom\'gol will send a message that the Horde is not to be trifled with.', 0),
(95775, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Kin\'weelay\'s hands shake as you hand him the rubbings.>$B$BThis is ancient Zandali but it is still legible, even to me. These four tablets speak of the ancient city, though I have never heard this account before.$B$BNor have I ever heard of the Loa of Tides. I thought all of the serpents depicted at the edges of the tablets were the loa Hethiss, but to my knowledge his avatar does not have a cobra hood or fins.$B$BCould this then be a depiction of the Loa of Tides? It almost looks more like a sea serpent.', 0),
(95776, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I see you have returned. I take it to mean you have slain their leader?$B$BGood. One less thing for us to worry about here. You have done well, <Class>.', 0),
(95787, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Four new tablets! This is fantastic news indeed.$B$BMy ancient Zandali is a bit rusty, but these legends seem to reference some... entity called The Loa of-$B$B<Loremaster Dibbs squints at the parchment.>$B$BTides? I-I don\'t recognize that title! Marvelous, $N! We may have stumbled upon a new loa!', 0),
(95788, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I am no mage, but even I can see how distinct these are from the fetishes I\'ve examined before. Their construction is more intricate in some ways, but more simple in others. They also seem to feature a great sea serpent of some kind.$B$BFascinating.$B$BWith what you have told me of the roaming undead, invading pirates, blood rituals and naga forces all converging on the ruins, it would seem I\'lalai is now a hotbed of many kinds of magic all being swirled together.$B$BThis certainly requires further study.', 0),
(95789, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent! I\'ll let the Baron know right away.$B$BAs promised, here\'s your share of the reward.', 0),
(95791, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I can\'t thank you enough! I will be able to sleep better knowing there are fewer of those Saltseers around.$B$BI know the Baron also appreciates your service. Here\'s your bounty.', 0),
(95793, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You persevere.$B$BPerhaps regrowth begins anew.', 0),
(95975, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh these are lovely! Gray got these for me? He\'s always such a ray of sunshine. It\'s no wonder our little Emma here misses him so much. She\'ll be so happy when he gets back.$B$BIsn\'t that right Emma? Daddy\'s coming home soon! Say daddy. Daddy.$B$B<The baby stops crying and spits up on her blankets.>$B$BIt\'s a start. Thank you for everything, $N. You\'ve been such a blessing. Feel free to visit us any time!', 0),
(95982, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Wow you sure know how to make something a dog would eat. No offense. Thanks for the help, pal.', 0),
(96010, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The crystals are in a few more pieces than I was expecting, but this looks to be all of it. I will hold onto these for the moment. Thank you, $N.$B$BYour next step will be to gather mana that is malleable enough to serve as both an adhesive for the broken pieces, and a conduit for the leylines to surge through thereafter.$B$BIt is quite a remarkable process, but gathering the mana may prove to be an inconvenience.', 0),
(96016, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, this be a powerful artifact, friend! I haven\'t crafted with some\'ting like this in a long time.$B$BYou take good care o\' dis now, ya hear? Looks like ya went through plenty to get it!', 0),
(96025, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You\'ve certainly earned quite the reputation here. Pleasure to finally meet you.', 0),
(96026, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Dese very heavy! Now me smash good rocks with heavy rocks!$B$B<Hamur crushes the rocks you collected into dust, leaving only the weightstones.>$B$BDese good for smashing. Here you go.', 0),
(96057, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.', 0),
(96059, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Enchanted Lute. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.', 0),
(96067, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Dang, the two of you really went at it! Couldn\'t have asked for a better show, and I got some great notes to boot.$B$BI\'ll fix up ol\' G45 here and make some changes to the engine. He\'ll be ready to go again in no time.$B$BTest, tweak, test, tweak. Such is the life of a great inventor.', 0),
(96076, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well done. My buyers will pay well for these. Enjoy the spoils!', 0),
(96082, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good work. That will suffice for now.$B$BAt least until their wounds re-open, or new soldiers get brought in...$B$B<Brother Lowley rubs his temples for a moment before re-adopting his stoic demeanor.>', 0),
(96083, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, so Brother Lowley sent you? Hard to believe he could spare the hands. That must mean you fulfilled your duties well.', 0),
(96084, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This looks... disgusting. What could be causing this sort of contamination?', 0),
(96104, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good find, <Class>. I will only need a moment to carve this into the proper shape.', 0),
(96108, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This is enough venom to kill a kodo in minutes--or a human in seconds. In either case, I am eager to put it to use.', 0),
(96109, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Arrows, poison, and a quiver to hold it all. You have made quite the hunter\'s kit here.$B$BPlease, take something in exchange for your labor. May it serve you well out in the field.', 0),
(96131, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Ketharas gently takes the staff and feather from you. He holds the feather in his palm for a moment and closes his eyes, then frowns deeply.>$B$BCome, <Class>, you must tell me all about this staff you have found.$B$BThis magic... I feel that this could be the beginning of a very important turning point for us here on the mountain. For good, perhaps? More likely, I fear, it is for ill.', 0),
(96135, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Can ye feel it, $N? The breeze sings of yer victory. If ye hadn\'t earned the elements\' respect before, ye sure have now.$B$BWalk tall, shaman. Yer a credit to our order.', 0);
INSERT INTO `everlake_forge_stage` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(96136, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'For the time being, I shall give you what you need to focus your spells and to call upon the spirits of air. Take this totem, and when you are ready, train with me some more.', 0),
(96138, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Merrick Valor, you say? Poor boy always wanted to prove himself. It was a shame what happened to him and his family.$B$BThank you for bringing this, $N. Perhaps it can shed some additional light on Raven Hill\'s history.', 0),
(96145, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have found the Shrine of Aviana, traveler, and we two--myself and Skylord Omnuron--are its last guardians.$B$BThe Wormwings would exterminate us if they could, but we defend this place with the grace of the sky goddess. Her dream lives on through us.', 0),
(96209, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What is this, little mortal? A branch? How curious...', 0),
(96252, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Though they may look like simple bangles to the outsider, each piece is a treasured part of our history, and an important part of a harpy\'s coming of age. Only those that have become adults may don ornamentations.$B$BThe blood smeared across them pains me, but it will help me remember the travesty that has occurred here. Hopefully when these are passed to the next generation, the weight of the lives lost will not be as heavy as it is today.$B$BThank you, <Class>.', 0),
(96262, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent! Aside from smelling wonderful, these pinecones have many uses, I assure you, such as adding to one\'s nest after a good cleaning. Gives it a bit extra, you know?$B$BThey also will be perfect for my plan, but I will get to that in a moment.$B$BAnyhow, excellent work, groundtreader! We\'re just about ready to enter phase two.', 0),
(96301, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The force with which the fel corruption was expunged from the heart, based on your description, is surprising. With this kinetic reaction, I fear we may have irreversibly fouled the well directly, tipping the scales against what equilibrium nature has struggled to temper after the great battle.$B$BEven a drop of poison, in a well of purity, can change the whole balance of nature.$B$BWe will have to keep this information guarded, and work to reverse this toxic tincture.', 0),
(96376, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Nazgrel\'s eyes widen when you show him the box of documents you recovered from Westfall.>$B$BWhat... where did you get these? Yes, the Warchief would be VERY interested in these documents.$B$BYou\'ve done a great service to the Horde, $N. Take this as a reward... and as appreciation for your silence, should anyone else ask you about these documents.', 0),
(96379, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Rix begins to visibly salivate as he looks at the contents of the document box that you recovered from Westfall.>$B$BGallywix\'s gullet, pal. This might just be the motherlode--er... I mean, uh, this is clearly just trash. You might even need to pay me to dispose of this garbage for you.$B$BTell you what, bub. Take this for the effort, and I\'ll get rid of this stuff for you. Don\'t try and haggle with me here either. I\'m really just doing you a favor here by taking this useless junk off your hands.', 0),
(96494, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Jobs done, then? I was almost concerned you weren\'t going to make it back.$B$BA Blackthorne presence that heavy indicates something more severe than we\'ve been estimating.', 0),
(96603, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you for your service to the Kirin Tor. Please continue to bring me any other such fragments of magic you find in your travels.$B$BYour service to the Kirin Tor will not go unnoticed.', 0),
(96609, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I hope you didn\'t have to kill too many of my misguided kin to recover these.$B$BI know this was quite the trek and I appreciate the effort. As promised, here is your reward.', 0),
(96616, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, thank you, <Class>. This is direly needed. Though it will not purge the infection, it will help ease the suffering as the infection takes its course.$B$BUnfortunately there is little else I can do for my fellows at this point but offer them wisdom and soothe their pain.', 0),
(96770, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you for your service to the Kirin Tor, $N. Here is your reward.$B$B<After handing you your reward, Archmage Lan\'dalock holds up the severed troll head and begins speaking to it.>$B$BYou and I are going to have a long conversation now, Zum\'rah. I\'m afraid you may not enjoy it.', 0),
(96772, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So the mage we detected was actually a black dragon in disguise? I can\'t say I\'m terribly surprised. Dragons are ever crafty. $B$BThe fact that you are standing here before me now suggests that you were forced to dispatch the dragon, yes? You\'ll get no complaints from me. You recovered the journal and there\'s one fewer villain in the world. That\'s a good day\'s work as far as I am concerned.$B$BThank you, $N.', 0),
(96773, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have done well. As promised, here is your reward.', 0),
(96774, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good goin\', <Class>. This be exactly what I\'m needin\'.$B$BLet\'s just keep this little transaction between us, ya? What Muln and the others don\'t know, won\'t be hurtin\' nobody!', 0),
(96775, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I be thankin\' you, <Class>. This a good thing you done for Ol\' Maz.$B$B<Mazu\'kon holds up the severed head and starts talking to it.>$B$BOh Zum\'rah, my old friend. I be tellin\' you this was comin\'. No more voodoo for you, mon.', 0),
(96776, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yes, this is what I saw in my vision. An\'she smiles upon us. This crystal will be a beacon for all those who wish to bathe in the radiance of the sun god.$B$BThank you, <Class>.', 0),
(96781, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It appears you\'ve some light fingers on you, $N. Very good.', 0),
(96782, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent. I will hold these in safekeeping, for now, while I decide what best to do with them.$B$BYou are dismissed, $N. Good work.', 0),
(96783, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Taking the uniform, you ready yourself for the next part of your mission.>', 0),
(96796, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I almost didn\'t notice you, I was in the middle of--Hey! You found one! I thought all the enchanted mithril bearings had been stolen already. That\'s why you\'re here, right?', 0),
(96797, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Danneth? I\'m sorry to tell you this but he\'s been missing for days. $B$BHis squad was ambushed near Serpent\'s Spine. We never recovered a body, but chances aren\'t good that he\'s still alive, I\'m afraid.', 0),
(96798, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Th-thank you, <Class>. I don\'t think I\'d have lasted long in this place alone. $B$BI\'m still too weak to fight, but if you are up to do the heavy lifting then we might be able to punch through these bastards and make it back to the keep.', 0),
(96800, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh you had to kill Doan to get the book back? Oh no...$B$B... well anyway, all\'s well that ends well! Thank you for returning this to its rightful place and helping me finish my thesis. I\'m quite convinced that reviving the lost art of dwarven rune magic is well within our grasp and I intend to prove it!$B$BIf only I could get into Grim Batol and inspect the runecarvings of old for myself...$B$BSomeday, perhaps.', 0),
(96811, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Knowing Danneth survived is a relief. He\'s a tough one.', 0),
(96830, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'If the sight of you wasn\'t enough, your words confirm it, then. Travelers have returned to Hyjal!$B$BThis warrior you met imparting mountain mercy is right--I have shared visions and sights during ancestral calling and channeling.$B$BThese flying terrors have become poisoned, worse to encounter than the demonic wings they replaced. We will stay on guard from the skies.', 0),
(96833, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I knew the chimaera were becoming more vicious with the change of every season out here, but bothering to try and carry off a full-grown human is the boldest they\'ve been yet. The sap is lucky to have the orc you spoke of around to show him mercy.$B$BYou say the venom was terribly corrosive, too? If the chimaera has been feeding on the fel-tainted beasts of the mountain, that would explain the bite of its maw being so vile.', 0),
(96874, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'These spines are tougher than I expected, $N! Crafting with them may not be as easy as I thought... but I\'ll keep working on it!', 0),
(96930, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Greetings again, Dirtwalker! You are still alive, it seems. It would also seem you\'ve talked to that oldstone-in-the-cave, Ketharas.$B$BSo, what have you learned since last we spoke, hmm?$B$B<The crow listens intently as you explain the journey Ketharas has sent you on thus far.>$B$BA mortal... did this? Yes, yes, yes. You will need the aid of the other gods of Hyjal, indeed. Luckily for you, I think I may know just the benevolent bird to get your flight started!', 0),
(96931, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, dirtwa-, I mean mortal! What has brought you to my domain?$B$B<Jereman listens to you as you recount your adventure on Hyjal with what appears to be a bemused expression.>$B$BI see you have met the brightest and most clever bird of my flock. She is, of course, beloved by all. Only second to myself, naturally.$B$BShe was right to send you to me. So, that oldstone needs to draw upon the power of the Wild Gods, does he? Very well, then.', 0),
(96939, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What have we here? A mortal? A living mortal at that. I have not seen one such as yourself in quite some time. I wonder what could possibly bring you to death\'s door.$B$B<Marrosis stares down his beak at you with a dour, almost tired expression.>$B$BOh. You were sent here by HER weren\'t you? I do hope she didn\'t accompany you.$B$B<He looks to the sky with the closest expression to a scowl a bird can make.>$B$BThe last thing I need is for that old crow to stick her talons in my business again.', 0),
(96957, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Marrosis looks pleased as he examines the bones you have brought him.>$B$BI enjoy the variety you have brought me, and I am sure my flock will as well.$B$BI thank you for your help here. Typically mortals fear death, but life and death are two sides of the same feather. I have met few mortals that are willing to help the way you have. You are welcome in my lands, and I will not forget what you have done for Hyjal.$B$BIf you must, you can report back to that dusty crow. I\'m sure she\'ll want the gossip.', 0),
(96964, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well, well, well. How unexpected! A mortal here on Hyjal that is willing to risk life and limb to come and visit me in my abode. What brings you to my lands, hmm?$B$B<Renalard\'s mischievous expression grows and he bares his teeth in what appears to be a wide grin.>$B$BAh, so it was Jereman who sent you! Well, why didn\'t you say so sooner? My, it has been some time since she came flapping about here last. Naturally I do have the answers to this little puzzle she has sent my way.', 0),
(96971, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ha HA! I watched you from here. Ah, to hoodwink a demon. It\'s not difficult, but it\'s always entertaining!$B$BNow that I have a whole pile of these supplies... well, you don\'t need to worry about that. I guarantee they\'ll be put to good use. You can thank me later!', 0),
(96978, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Stay back, wielder of fire and metal! Perhaps you are accustomed to my kind being your prey, but no more!$B$BJereman is not the only god on this mountain. Take care, mortal, lest you cross a power greater than your own. You meddle in the affairs of gods at your own peril!', 0),
(96982, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent, $N. I can see in your eyes that you have made a choice.$B$BI am happy to be able to provide you with one of our fine kodo. I must say the one you have picked seems fond of you already. I hope you will take good care of it, and it of you.$B$BMay the Earthmother guide you both.', 0),
(96989, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, good. I be seein\' in your eyes that you have made a choice. A fine one at that.$B$BDe one you have picked seems fond of you already, though I am not surprised. I hope you two be taking good care of each other out there in de world.$B$BBlessings of Gonk go wit ya both.', 0),
(96991, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Galvinquam\'s bags will join the other gear we\'re restoring. I see he carried more than he thought--there are tools tucked in here that will serve us as we rebuild.$B$BYou\'ve eased his journey and given us time to prepare a proper welcome for one raised on the low plains. The mountain asks much of those who climb it for the first time.$B$BThanks to you, his heart will meet the summit with strength left to give.', 0),
(96992, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good eye, $N. Picking these out of the rubble saves them from slowly rusting away. Now they can rust away in this glorified lean-to! Ha!$B$BThanks, I mean it. I\'ll put these to use, though I\'ll probably have to scrounge even more to get the walls finished.', 0),
(96994, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Ogunaro gives you a satisfied grunt.>$B$BIt seems you have found your companion. I am happy to see they have finally found their rider.$B$BTake good care of them, <Class>, and in return they will take care of you. Never forget your friendship.$B$BI wish both of you well in your adventures. Go forth to victory!', 0),
(96996, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent, $N. I can see in your eyes that you have made a choice.$B$BI must say the one you have picked seems fond of you already, and it will be nice to have a reminder of home with you as your adventures take you far from Zephras. I hope you will take good care of it, and it of you.$B$BWinds guide you both!', 0),
(96997, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent, <Class>. I can see you have made a choice.$B$BWhile many creatures will die and wither, this unholy steed does not need to stop for rest nor food. Even so, do take care of it out there in the world, and hopefully it will take care of you in turn.$B$BThough it is dead, the bond you share is real enough. Even in undeath we must all find our purpose.$B$BI wish you well on your adventures. Dark Lady watch over you both.', 0),
(96999, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Dis... dis be his. My big brudda, Qujo. So many seasons gone by, an\' da cloth still hold his mark. Da spirits be kind to leave somethin\' behind.$B$BMy brudda walked da old paths wit\' pride. He hunted so others could sleep.$B$BYa bring him home when ya bring dis back. Dat matter. More den gold, more den words.$B$BSen\'jin gonna honor both ya names \'round the fire tonight.', 0),
(97009, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'A worthy offering.$B$BWicked protrusions--horns, spines, armor--shatter into cruel shards. Even in ruin, they hunger to wound.$B$BI will bind these spikes and enhance them with my own runic fire. Let the Legion feel their own strength turned against them. Let them feel the fear that they have struck into the hearts of mortal races.$B$BTheir pain is my purpose.', 0),
(97017, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, that one is a great companion and will do ye well, $N.$B$BI\'m proud to be the one able to send you and your ram on yer way. Seems to me that the ram ye picked seems fond of you already. I hope you\'ll take good care of it, and it of you.$B$BDon\'t forget to drop by sometime! I\'d love to hear about yer adventures together.', 0),
(97018, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ho there, <Class>! I\'m happy to see you\'ve completed your training with ol\' Ultham. I\'m glad he sent you my way!', 0),
(97045, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent, $N! I can see you\'ve made a choice, and what a fine pick it is.$B$BI\'m proud to be able to provide you with one of our horses. I must say the one you have picked seems fond of you already! I hope you will take good care of it, and it of you.$B$BCome back if you ever need new horseshoes! They\'re on the house.', 0),
(97046, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Excellent, $N, most excellent indeed! You have made a great choice.$B$BThe biometrics are all set up and the mechanostrider seems excited to get its system processes started. I hope you both will take care of one another out there in the vast world!$B$BCome back if you ever need a tune-up!', 0),
(97049, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Mmm, how interesting! It seems to have some kind of rejuvenating effect even on rotted skin. It appears to make the skin look less withered or aged. It obviously does not change the rotted nature but this is still quite noteworthy.$B$BI will need to inform my colleagues right away!$B$BOh, yes. Here is your coin, now be on your way. I have experiments to run.$B$B<Chemist Fuely makes a dismissive motion with his hand as he turns back to his experiments.>', 0),
(97074, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Greetings, <Class>! I\'m happy to see you\'ve completed your training with Jartsam. I\'m glad he sent you my way!', 0),
(97130, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you for recovering this. Lan\'dalock and I have long debated the nature of Gurubashi blood magic. An artifact such as this should be invaluable in helping us better understand this primal magic.', 0),
(97170, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hello, <Class>! I\'m happy to see you\'ve completed your training with Randal. I\'m glad he sent you my way!', 0),
(97188, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hello, <Class>! I\'m happy to see you\'ve completed your training with my brother Binjy. I\'m glad he sent you my way!', 0),
(97194, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Throm\'ka, <Class>. I\'m happy to see you\'ve completed your training with Kildar.$B$BHe is masterful at handling these wolves and helping one learn the bond between wolf and rider. Riding one of these beautiful creatures isn\'t for the faint of heart.', 0),
(97196, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This will do nicely. We\'ve deprived our enemies of an important tool, and equipped ourselves with a powerful weapon to use against the Scourge.', 0),
(97197, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh thank you, $N! I am eager to begin studying this sample!', 0),
(97198, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you for your efforts here, $N. I\'m sure that it was not easy to recover this totem, and the Earthen Ring is in your debt.', 0),
(97200, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Spirits be with ya, <Class>. I\'m happy to see you\'ve completed your training with Xar\'Ti.$B$BShe is masterful at handling these raptors and helping one learn the bond between raptor and rider. Riding one of these beautiful creatures ain\'t be for the faint of heart.', 0),
(97203, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah hello, <Class>. I\'m pleased to see you\'ve completed your training with Velma.$B$BShe has a way with these creatures that few others do. If you have trained with her you will have no issues with any of our steeds here in Brill.', 0),
(97204, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah hello, <Class>. I\'m happy to see you\'ve completed your training with Kar.$B$BIf you have trained with him you will go with the Earthmother\'s guidance. He has a way with these kodo that few others do. He is the best riding teacher in all of Mulgore.', 0),
(97205, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Marvelous! You have done a fantastic job. Learning how to ride one of these striders often takes patience and a steady hand.$B$BThey do not flee by nature, but who knows what things you and your mount will face out there in the greater world? Yes, it is best to be prepared!', 0),
(97257, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It is done. The Eternal Flame burns once again.$B$BYour trial is now complete. I am pleased to present you with your Fire Totem. Use this icon of power well in your travels, $N. $B$BJust remember, the power of the elemental plane serves those that respect it, and consumes those who do not. This is our way.', 0),
(97284, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good work. With all your efforts against those fools at Thunder Axe, surely they will think twice before ransacking another caravan passing through.$B$BWith any luck, they\'ll cower behind their gates for long enough to die out on their own.', 0),
(97319, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'In retrospect, coming here was probably a bad idea.', 0),
(97332, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Huh? What you got for me?$B$B<Whizzbuzz peeks inside the crate and his expression immediately lights up with surprise.>$B$BLook\'t this! Lozgil finally pulled through. It only took a scathing letter and payin\' the courier to threaten him to get the point across. Wonder what his excuse is. Did the ship\'s captain get captured? Did a zeppelin crash?$B$BHaha, could you imagine? We don\'t even have a zeppelin tower around here!$B$BYou look like you went through a lot to deliver this, so have a reward.', 0),
(97378, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have done well, $N.$B$BI know this was no easy task, but with this one life taken many more will be saved.', 0),
(97386, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'They may not have looked like they were ready to make an assault on Grom\'gol, but it was a risk we could not afford to make again.$B$BFor the Horde!', 0),
(97405, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Is it done? Sheesh, I sure hope so. I don\'t think Gnaz realizes that if we anger the ogres enough that they\'ll march all the way up here and rip his little race cart to pieces!$B$BThank you, I can breathe a sigh of relief now.$B$B<Knaz does, indeed, breathe a sigh of relief.>', 0),
(97490, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You took down Hailspite! Alright, let\'s take a look at that... moss.$B$BThis stuff ain\'t bad at all, now that I have it up close. It\'s colder than a handful of snow, but doesn\'t melt!$B$BI\'ve gotta try this out...$B$BThanks buddy.', 0),
(97540, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Let\'s continue on to Torta.', 0),
(97617, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Fantastic! This is more than enough to make the case to send folks back to the Badlands. I know everyone has their sights on Uldaman proper, but we can\'t let that distract us from the inevitable wealth of discoveries to be made all around the plains.$B$BI trust you scared off who or whatever had taken over those spots, right? Sure hope so, else the boss is going to chew my ear off for lying about their safety...', 0),
(97884, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you, <Class>. I very much doubt I would have survived the journey or destination, considering the state you say Sunnyglade is in now.$B$BThis tome is exactly what I needed. I am happy to say all of the pages are here as well.$B$BPerhaps I can learn a new trade in undeath. It would give me a skill to hone for the rest of my unlife, at least.', 0),
(97918, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.', 0),
(97930, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.', 0),
(97937, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.', 0),
(97950, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.', 0),
(97954, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Reagent Bot. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.', 0),
(97963, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Mana Well. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.', 0),
(97986, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Are we finally gettin\' some reinforcements?$B$BLight\'s Hope sent ya? It\'s true, we see the worst cases in all the Plaguelands at this small post.', 0),
(98027, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh my! I can\'t believe you found this. I thought I had looked everywhere!$B$BI had lost it when I went to deliver supplies to one of our outposts, but after searching along the road I had given up.$B$BThank you for bringing this back to me. It was a gift from my late parents, and I can\'t express how much it means to have it back.', 0),
(98071, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'That\'s the hops smell I missed! Ye done me a great favor, $N, takes me days to leave every time I make the trip to Dun Garok myself. Hard to pull me self outta the halls o\' that fortress once I get comfortable.$B$BHappy to keep some old tastes on the shelf for fellow dwarves.$B$BHave a little somethin\' for helpin out.', 0),
(98109, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Not... what I expected a visit about. $B$BI do recognize this fabric. It\'s of Shen\'Dorei origin. You found this in Thondroril river?$B$BHmm...', 0),
(98192, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'These good! You get good scale hides. We no run out soon.$B$BWhen last time we ran out we not have enough to cover one ogre. Many us not have cover then.$B$BOrc friends not like that. They say so, very much, a lot.', 0),
(98208, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'It has survived! Oh, Elune be praised!$B$BA thousand thanks, $N. If you are willing, I do have one more favor to ask of you...', 0),
(98233, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'By the Light, that smells awful! I have no idea how I am going to get that foul odor off of this blade.$B$BOh great. Now I\'ve gotten the ooze all over myself as well.$B$BWell, thank you for getting my sword back, $N. I endeavor to repay the favor someday.$B$BPreferably when I smell better than I do now.', 0),
(98246, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'They\'re not for me plan--they\'re to feed Bassbeak. She\'s of no help at all if she\'s hungry, trust me. She might be more dangerous than the orcs if she\'s ticked off!$B$BUntainted food can be hard to come by in these lands as of late...', 0),
(98284, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'There you have it, you can now craft your very own Enchanted Lute. Most folk don\'t care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you\'ll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.$B$BOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You\'ll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven\'t already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.', 0),
(98325, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Warlord Goretooth grins.>$B$BYou have your orders.', 0),
(98435, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, no wonder there is such joy running through the streams of Mulgore. You have done a great service today. The wells provide much for not only our people, but to the wildlife we depend on for food, clothing, and companionship.$B$BIt is my humble pleasure to honor Mull\'s request. Please, accept this token of my gratitude.', 0),
(98477, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Thank you for your service to the Earthen Ring. Please continue to bring me any other such fragments of magic you find in your travels.$B$BYour service to the Earthen Ring will not go unappreciated.', 0),
(98576, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Da magic dat flows through you be da greatest power in da universe, but ya must be patient. Wait for da perfect moment to strike. Choose da right response to da problem at hand. If you be smart, and you watch carefully, dere be nothing you can\'t do.$B$BWhen ya tink you be ready for trainin\', come back to Mai\'ah. She teach you what you ready to learn, no problem.', 0),
(98903, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Theramore Expeditionary Force are grateful for your dedication and prowess in the battle for the Darkspear Islands, $N.$B$BFor the Alliance!', 0),
(99193, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, $N!', 0),
(99194, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Fantastic--these will go right to use, I assure you. Thank you again for your assistance! We\'d certainly be lost without you.$B$BWith all the donations you\'ve made, I would certainly process any additional runecloth donations you care to make in the future.$B$BJust be sure to check in with me, and I\'ll personally make sure that your good deeds won\'t go unrecognized!', 0),
(99198, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, $N!', 0),
(99199, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Fantastic--these will go right to use, I assure you. Thank you again for your assistance! We\'d certainly be lost without you.$B$BWith all the donations you\'ve made, I would certainly process any additional runecloth donations you care to make in the future. Just be sure to check in with me, and I\'ll personally make sure that your good deeds won\'t go unrecognized!', 0),
(99257, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You were successful, I see! And what a heart you recovered. I am excited to know that the passing of centuries did little to tarnish the craftsmanship of this gemstone.$B$BMost importantly, this is a promising discovery. It would seem that, indeed, mana is temporary, but gemstones are forever.$B$BAre you eager to learn what comes next?', 0),
(99670, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Underwing!$B$BI owe you a debt of gratitude it seems, my young friend. I admit I may have gotten in a bit over my wings with that last adventure. It may seem we Wild Gods are aloof, but we are immortal spirits of the wilds. Many threats do little to scare us. $B $BHaving experienced what happened to Velician first-talon however, I now know the danger lurking right under our beaks.$B$BI must account for the other demigods at Hyjal\'s summit. They have been too silent, and I fear the worst.', 0);
INSERT INTO `quest_offer_reward` (`ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild`) SELECT `ID`, `Emote1`, `Emote2`, `Emote3`, `Emote4`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `EmoteDelay4`, `RewardText`, `VerifiedBuild` FROM `everlake_forge_stage`;
INSERT IGNORE INTO `everlake_import_rows` (`tbl`, `k1`, `k2`, `k3`, `k4`, `file`, `note`) SELECT 'quest_offer_reward', s.`ID`, 0, 0, 0, '2026_11_16_900_world_everlake_forge_00035_import.sql', 'Forge #35 (import)' FROM `everlake_forge_stage` s;
INSERT INTO `everlake_forge_stage` (`ID`, `EmoteOnComplete`, `EmoteOnIncomplete`, `EmoteOnCompleteDelay`, `EmoteOnIncompleteDelay`, `CompletionText`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
(8152, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What do ya need? A tourniquet?', 0),
(78089, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You bring news from Kalimdor?', 0),
(78090, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You\'re a long way from the cathedral, paladin. I hope you realize you have no authority here.', 0),
(78830, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How goes the hunt? Surely the bird hasn\'t got you beat!', 0),
(79358, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What\'ve ye brought me?', 0),
(80411, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Go now, time is of the essence.', 0),
(82084, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Those spellbook materials will take you on quite a journey!', 0),
(83934, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Whatcha got for me, <Race>?', 0),
(84377, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I\'m well aware of your recent whereabouts, $N.$B$BDo you have something to show me?', 0),
(86577, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'We must get to the bottom of the corruption that is turning Felwood into a demon-haunted wilderness!', 0),
(86615, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I need those papers!', 0),
(86616, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The less those Vilebranch trolls are disrupting the flow of the elements, the simpler it will be to commune with the elementals.', 0),
(86620, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Don\'t startle the young ones!', 0),
(87295, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Sure is hot today, isn\'t it?', 0),
(89001, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Got the supplies yet?', 0),
(89013, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good luck gettin\' that honey. If the wasps start swarmin\' ye, my advice is to jump in the water!', 0),
(89228, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Got that squid yet? I\'m gettin\' a bit peckish now that I\'m talkin\' about it.', 0),
(90647, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What brings you to the summit, <Class>?', 0),
(90750, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yes?', 0),
(90865, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Tread carefully. Their eyes are upon us.', 0),
(91488, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Do you have those hides yet, <Class>? I see rain clouds forming in the sky...', 0),
(91531, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You say you bring news from Azshara? Don\'t tell me that Ag\'tor and the others are dead!', 0),
(91547, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Jediga sent you? This ought to be good.', 0),
(91568, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'They say the richest goblin in a gold rush is the one selling shovels. I figured if I made my own I could hedge my bets.', 0),
(91569, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Trust me, $N, you don\'t wanna miss out on what I\'ve got planned.', 0),
(91608, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'If the wasps swarm you, do not run back here. Ag\'tor would have my hide!', 0),
(91685, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Izvi is rubbing her hands in anticipation>$B$BWhaddya got for me, $N? Did the wand work?', 0),
(91754, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you got a bunch of rich, verdant soil? You can find it all over the south side of the valley, where rainfall runs down the slopes and brings runoff with it. It forms mulch with the fallen leaves from the trees and collects in the shade beneath them.', 0),
(91755, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How many Verdant Leaves have you found? Those shrubberies are dangerous, but the only way to get the medicinal plant matter is to take it from the plants!', 0),
(91770, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, greetings again, little one. Excuse me... if I am not... sociable. The fel taint that afflicts Hyjal... festers in my very roots and bark. These old wounds of mine, they burn... they seep... I only wish to sleep.', 0),
(91794, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You brought me some symbols to show off?', 0),
(91883, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you found Zarrat? Her cunning is considerable.', 0),
(91923, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you found Celastrus?', 0),
(92011, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Kaylaena is talking to herself while searching her workshop.>$B$B...Where did I put that micro-spanner? $B$BOh don\'t mind me, I\'ve already stabilized the mana cells. The spanner\'s for the NEXT job!', 0),
(92014, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Don\'t mind if you keep the finest furs for yourself, but any nine tails will do.', 0),
(92016, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Well is a font of miraculous magic, but that wondrous magic can be twisted and perverted. With such great power, comes greater danger.', 0),
(92017, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hippogryphs may yield their feathers without difficulty, but be cautious--the chimaera are prone to corruption, being drawn to the sulfurous vapors. They can be twice as vicious as the smaller birds.', 0),
(92020, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What\'s this book?', 0),
(92069, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'To slay either beast would be the feat of a lifetime for most hunters. To defeat both will take all your might and cunning.', 0),
(92147, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You can find the nests of the Wormwings all over this plateau. Bring me their feathers as proof of your strikes against them.', 0),
(92169, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Can I help you?', 0),
(92317, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Were you able to meet with Jereman? Hopefully her mischief has led you to answers instead of more questions.', 0),
(92335, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How fares your search for something to aid our work?', 0),
(92344, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The furbolg have my sympathies, and I wish your discovery came under more auspicious circumstances. Truthfully, however, we cannot pass up this opportunity to harness the power of Nordrassil.', 0),
(92446, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How goes da hunt?', 0),
(92500, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How fares your search for something to aid our work?', 0),
(92519, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'If you can get them something for the pain, you can have some of these patients back out the door as fast as they walk in.', 0),
(92533, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Do not carry their cursed weaponry long, we do not yet know what affliction is possible by mere handling.', 0),
(92591, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'We will never be safe until the reanimator is destroyed!', 0),
(92592, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'We will never be safe until da reanimator is destroyed!', 0),
(92593, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Johun is dripping sweat and looks like he\'s already had an extremely long day.>', 0),
(92609, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You be findin\' dem nice, long feathers now, hm?', 0),
(92612, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Did you need something?', 0),
(92702, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The gnome\'s parachute is badly tangled in the branches of the tree.', 0),
(92743, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'No crown, no talk!', 0),
(92755, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Our clan draws most of our power from the Tears of Theradras, many of which you may have seen scattered about the walls of the khan\'s cave. But as time passes, some are lost, destroyed, or simply depleted.$B$BThese types of reagents are new to me, though the enchantments themselves are not.', 0),
(92814, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Your assistance here would be like impaling two Magram on one pike! You aid the Gelkis in our war effort, and you help Halea improve her skills.', 0),
(92817, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You may have all the time in the world, outsider, but my kind is in the midst of war. If you intend to help, do hurry.', 0),
(92818, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I SAID HURRY UP.', 0),
(92844, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'For every bone short you are for the task, I will take one of yours to make up the difference.', 0),
(92847, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'These staves may be the missing piece we need to secure the rest of the Valley of Bones. Go now, <Race>, let us make use of the Gelkis\' ways before their next discovery.', 0),
(92859, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I\'m so excited about the alchemical possibilities that this presents!', 0),
(92873, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Despite your aid thus far, if you are unable to raise the dead then your usefulness with the Magram has come to an end.', 0),
(92878, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<Blaise points insistently at the note he gave you.>', 0),
(92911, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How\'s the project coming, $N?', 0),
(92960, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Find anything peculiar?', 0),
(93041, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I did not expect to see you back so soon. Is this a bad omen?', 0),
(93122, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Back already, $N? What is the word?', 0),
(93129, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Slay their soldiers and starve the survivors. Their little hideaway should never be a sufficient staging ground against our clan again!', 0),
(93197, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You look like you got something for me!', 0),
(93226, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What business does an outsider have with Gorhak?', 0),
(93269, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you finished the trip?', 0),
(93406, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How goes the search for the missing mail? I bet those yetis in the hills near here have it!', 0),
(93407, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The sting of the thorns is a small price to pay now, so that we may assure our future security.', 0),
(93465, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Our interests are rather well aligned, $N. By slaying Gimashi, you will have your answers, and I will have one less villain to worry about.', 0),
(93663, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You bring a delivery from Stonard? Well, let me see it then.', 0),
(93678, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You spoke to the mage? What answers did he have for you?', 0),
(93759, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How goes the foraging?', 0),
(94222, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'AHHH! Oh... Me thought you look like slime monster.', 0),
(94231, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hey, HEY, man, haven\'t you heard of a little thing called \"subtlety\"? Spell it out with me, S-U-B...LETY. You\'re going to blow my cover!', 0),
(94241, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'WHAT???', 0),
(94256, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hello, skyborne! That twinkle in your eye makes me guess you have a special delivery!', 0),
(94615, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I\'m itching just as much as ol\' Demar to find out what happened to the horses. They\'re how I make my living, after all.', 0),
(94792, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You will learn, $N, and one day you will be a great hunter.', 0),
(94858, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I\'m not holding out hope that there\'s much left, but I need to know.', 0),
(94863, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'With learning, $N, comes mastery.', 0),
(94890, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What better report is there than total victory?', 0),
(94891, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You had a successful venture, I trust?', 0),
(94894, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Word from Farholde, is it? After all this time has the Knight Commander finally seen reason?', 0),
(94925, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The lions hunt in packs, <Class>. Be careful not to get surrounded.', 0),
(94929, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yes? What... what is that musky smell? It\'s horrendous.', 0),
(94981, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you gathered the materials?', 0),
(94982, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Has the threat been eliminated?', 0),
(94983, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well? What have you found?', 0),
(94984, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Find anything of interest?', 0),
(95027, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Watch for the Hyjal owls flying in the trees. They\'re white! Easy to spot against all of the green and brown.', 0),
(95123, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Got that gunpowder yet?', 0),
(95261, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'When we catch that thing...oh ho...no one\'ll be laughing at ol\' Argo then!', 0),
(95267, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Is it...is that monster dead yet...?', 0),
(95296, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Shipment from Powderfuse Port, huh? And from Friz no less. Good luck with that, buddy. You gotta wake up pretty early in the mornin\' to pull that one over me!', 0),
(95317, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Blech, the smells coming out of that area burn my nostrils. It seems like there are four separate areas functioning in that warlock camp, but I can\'t get close enough to make out what they\'re doing.$B$BHopefully you\'ll be able to find something that will tell us what they are doing here. These demon casters don\'t seem very smart.$B$BWhatever they\'re doing, it certainly isn\'t natural, which is all the more reason to get them on their way quickly.', 0),
(95319, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Did you bring me the crystals?', 0),
(95378, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You\'re back? Already?$B$BDid you slay them?$B$BIt felt like the wards of the cage dispelled but I\'ve been in here so long it\'s hard to tell. Especially with all of this fel energy around.', 0),
(95380, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Is that you, dirtwalker? You look awful and much more slime-covered than before.$B$BHopefully you\'ve brought the slime though, yes?', 0),
(95383, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Uck, you don\'t have to tell me where you\'re from. I can smell Powderfuse Port all over you.', 0),
(95426, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'So...? Any luck with those supplies?', 0),
(95472, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Lackey? Why are you givin\' me this...', 0),
(95511, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you made your choice? These sabers are of the highest quality and have been bred in Darnassus for generations.$B$BYou will not find a more loyal companion.', 0),
(95568, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'While the plants on Hyjal struggle to survive in the face of fel corruption, you should be able to find blossoming life if you look to the undergrowth.', 0),
(95569, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you found any abandoned owl eggs?', 0),
(95613, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I know a few candles are a small gesture in the grand scheme of what we\'re doing here, but just as I care for the living, so too must I care for the dead.', 0),
(95770, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You\'ve returned! Were you able to find anything? What did you learn of the naga presence?', 0),
(95776, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I will admit I foster no shortage of loathing for the naga, though I do admire their tenacity and strength.$B$BThey are a foe worthy of my blade.', 0),
(95787, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I wonder if my friends in the Explorer\'s League have gotten wind of this risen island--$B$BOh! $N, you\'ve returned. Did you visit the troll ruins? Did you find any new legends?', 0),
(95788, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you traveled to the fabled Drowned City? What did you find?$B$BCome, I want to hear everything you saw in exact detail, if you have the time.', 0),
(95789, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Heya! Have you had a chance to take care of those blasted pirates yet? I have a crew standing by to go plunder-- er, explore the troll ruins.', 0),
(95791, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Man, those ships are creepy.$B$BThe Saltseer pirates seem to have this ability to navigate the seas in a way I ain\'t ever seen before. It ain\'t natural! It\'s almost as if the ship is alive. I\'ve seen the pirates aboard walk away from the steering wheel and the ship seems to drive itself!$B$BI\'d rather not know how they accomplished that. Feels like dark magic to me.', 0),
(95793, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Every demon that falls brings us one step closer to peace within these mountains.', 0),
(95975, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Good to see you again, $N. Did you find my husband?', 0),
(95982, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You get the grub? The wolves are startin\' to look hungry...', 0),
(96010, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I would rather not further draw the centaur\'s attention toward me or my fallen kin, else I would seek out the crystals myself.', 0),
(96016, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Great battle with de elements, mm? Tings turned out how they was always meant to.$B$BBut since you here, what brings you to ol\' Bath\'rah?', 0),
(96057, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Come talk to me again once you\'ve gained some skill with your profession.', 0),
(96059, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yes, I can teach you.', 0),
(96067, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I should clarify that I can\'t be held personally responsible for any injuries you suffer during the stress test.', 0),
(96076, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You fetch me those elven curios yet?', 0),
(96082, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How fare the soldiers?', 0),
(96084, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Without knowing the root cause of their illness, I can only do so much to treat these people.', 0),
(96135, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I can feel the storm in my belly, $N. Have ye dispersed it yet?', 0),
(96138, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yes, what is it?', 0),
(96252, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I mourn that my sisters\' blood had not even cooled before these prized possessions were ripped from their bodies.', 0),
(96262, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Caw?$B$BAh, there seems to be a distinct pine-y freshness about you! Did you gather the pinecones I asked for?$B$B<The crow tilts her head to the side looking amused.>', 0),
(96301, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The potency of the Well of Eternity, and its various effects, seem to always be shifting.', 0),
(96376, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<It occurs to you that as an advisor to the Warchief, Nazgrel might be very interested to see the documents you\'ve recovered from Westfall. Ask him if any of these documents make any sense to him.>', 0),
(96379, 0, 0, 0, 0, '<It occurs to you that a goblin who deals in asset recovery might be very interested to see the documents you\'ve recovered from Westfall. Ask him if any of these documents make any sense to him... and more importantly, what he might be willing to pay you for them.>', 0),
(96603, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This disturbance of magic has us all extremely concerned. So significant was the magical disruption that the arcane barrier that has protected Dalaran during our reconstruction suddenly became impossible to maintain. We have erected lesser wards, but this has still left us dangerously vulnerable.$B$BIt\'s our hope that we are able to determine the cause of this disruption soon. Any help you provide in this endeavor will surely increase your standing and esteem in the eyes of the Kirin Tor.', 0),
(96609, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'My wayward people are on a course of action that will lead them to ruin, and I have little desire to return home to Silvermoon to witness how far we\'ve fallen firsthand.$B$BHowever, I must confess that I miss some of the finer things that my homeland has to offer.', 0),
(96616, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you brought the herbs? My eyesight isn\'t what it used to be after the war, and after my injury I am not as stable on my feet as I once was as a young orc.$B$B<Ortak smiles sadly.>$B$BSuch is the price of war and time.', 0),
(96770, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Troll necromancy is an insidious art and only those trolls with a particularly sick and twisted disposition practice it. Little does Zum\'rah know that he isn\'t the only one who can animate the dead, and losing his head is only the beginning of his troubles.', 0),
(96772, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Did you recover the journal?', 0),
(96773, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The methods and means of the members of the scourge are mysterious and esoteric, even to the educated mages of the Kirin Tor. Some speculate that their magic is akin to elemental magic in nature, perhaps some force that acts as the antithesis of the light.$B$BSome speculate that their magic is drawn from the spirit realm itself via small tears in the veil between life and death. The more scourge artifacts we can recover intact for study, the more complete our understanding will be.', 0),
(96774, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How you doin\' mon? Job done yet?', 0),
(96775, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Bad voodoo is bad for ya. Remember that, mon.', 0),
(96776, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'An\'she is the physical manifestation of the sun\'s radiance. Some say he is the right eye of the Earthmother, and a force of pure, cleansing light. Without An\'she, the shu\'halo would live forever in darkness and despair. $B$BI have devoted myself to the sun god\'s service and hope to spread his light to all of our people in time.', 0),
(96781, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'What are they after in those ruins, I wonder?', 0),
(96782, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Odds are we shall have those heirlooms before Barton even notices his reports are missing.', 0),
(96796, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Now where did I put the toroid converter...', 0),
(96800, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Sometimes I feel like this thesis is cursed.', 0),
(96957, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you collected the bones I asked for? I am sure it seems like an odd request.$B$BAdmittedly it is much slower for one such as myself to collect them. There are only so many bones I can delicately grasp in my talons before I accidentally crush them to powder.$B$B<Marrosis sighs, looking annoyed.>$B$BBefore you ask; no, I have no intention of building some kind of shrine. That was HER suggestion. That is the last time I ask for any ideas from her or her flock.', 0),
(96971, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Oh, you\'re back already? Did you have a chance to use that fox fur I gave you? I promise the results will be amusing.$B$B<Renalard grins at you with a mouth filled with too many teeth.>', 0),
(96982, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you made your choice? These kodos have carried our ancestors across the plains for generations. They are a steadfast and mighty beast.$B$BYou will not find a more loyal and noble mount for your travels.', 0),
(96989, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have ya made ya choice? We trolls have been huntin\' with raptors since the dawn of time. There is no bond deeper than that between a troll and their raptor.$B$BRiding these beautiful predators be one of the most impressive things any Darkspear could be hoping to master. Many be trying to subdue or befriend them, but many be losing their lives instead.$B$BOnce bonded though, ya be hard pressed to find a more loyal and lethal companion.', 0),
(96991, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'If you\'re looking for a place to rest, try the remains of the inn just down the road south of here.', 0),
(96992, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Fine joinery? These saws are not the kind of quality tools for that. We\'re not going for a thousand-year structure here, after all.', 0),
(96994, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you inspected the wolves? The bond between orc and wolf is one older than time. Ours is a bond that transcends generations and now even worlds.$B$BI have even heard tale that some riders know their wolf\'s name upon bonding.$B$BYou will not find a more fierce and loyal companion.', 0),
(96996, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you made your choice? These striders are said to have been blessed by the very winds themselves. However, I believe, like most creatures on Zephras, they have adapted to our elemental home by being infused with the elements within Skywall.$B$BBut who is to say, perhaps it is both! Either way, I feel more connected to the winds when I ride mine.', 0),
(96999, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Life by da sea? Shore be nice.', 0),
(97009, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Demons are meant to be slain. With their own cruel implements we will hasten their deaths.', 0),
(97017, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Back already are ye? Have you made your choice then?$B$BThese rams can be stubborn, but there ain\'t a finer beast this side of the mountains. Almost nothin\' fazes them!$B$BYe won\'t find a more sturdy companion.', 0),
(97018, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Once ya learn how to ride a ram, you\'ll be able to go on journeys with your mount all over the world! It\'s certainly faster than running everywhere.', 0),
(97045, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You\'ve returned! Have you made your choice? These horses are some of the finest this side of the Eastern Kingdoms.$B$BYou won\'t find a more courageous steed.', 0),
(97046, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you made your choice? These mechanostriders are of the highest quality and have been handcrafted by the finest engineers in Gnomeregan! Er, Ironforge I suppose.$B$BThey are far more reliable than any beast. They don\'t have sentience, but they do have individual quirks, mostly due to the difference in their construction by different engineers. Still, it\'s largely a color preference.', 0),
(97049, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Hello, can I help you?$B$BOh, yes, $N. Have you collected the Seeping Slime Essence I asked about?', 0),
(97074, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Once you learn how to ride a saber, you will be able to go on journeys with your mount all over the world!$B$BIt\'s certainly faster than running everywhere, I assure you.', 0),
(97130, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Gurubashi blood magic is most distasteful, but still highly fascinating. Did you know that the ancient troll empires would periodically initiate a ritual known as the \"Blood Moon\" that would deliberately induce an insatiable madness and bloodlust on their entire population?$B$BWhy deliberately inflict a period of merciless bedlam and carnage on your people? To what end? It\'s deeply fascinating in an academic sense, but I shudder to think of how brutal life must have been in such a culture.', 0),
(97170, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Once you learn how to ride a horse, you\'ll be able to go on journeys with your mount all over the world.$B$BIt\'s certainly faster than running everywhere. Though, I won\'t stop you if that is your preference.', 0),
(97188, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Once you learn how to pilot a mechanostrider, you\'ll be able to go on journeys with your mount all over the world!$B$BIt\'s certainly faster than running everywhere. Though, I won\'t stop you if that is your preference.', 0),
(97194, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Once you learn how to ride a wolf you\'ll be able to go on journeys with your mount all over the world.$B$BIt\'s certainly faster than running everywhere. Though, I won\'t stop you if that is your preference.', 0),
(97196, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Death\'s Head quilboar have been a constant thorn in our side for years, due in no small part to machinations of that accursed Lich.', 0),
(97197, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The concept of a towering giant made entirely of molten rock is both thrilling and terrifying to me.', 0),
(97198, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Elemental magic is neither evil, nor good, but it simply reflects the will of the one who channels it. Studying the tools and methods of those who seek to corrupt the natural order will help us become ever more effective at doing battle against such forces.', 0),
(97200, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Once ya be learnin\' to ride a raptor, you\'ll be able to go on journeys with your mount all over the world!$B$BThere ain\'t be anything more liberating than feelin\' the ground rush by while on the back of one of these creatures.$B$BIt\'s certainly faster than running everywhere. Though, I won\'t be stoppin\' ya if that is your preference.', 0),
(97203, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Once you learn how to ride a skeletal horse, you\'ll be able to go on journeys with your mount all over the world.$B$BIt\'s certainly faster than running everywhere. Though, I won\'t stop you if that is your preference.', 0),
(97204, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Once you learn how to ride a kodo, you\'ll be able to go on journeys with your mount all over the world.$B$BIt\'s certainly faster than running everywhere. Though, I won\'t stop you if that is your preference.', 0),
(97205, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Once you learn how to ride a galestrider, you\'ll be able to go on journeys with your mount all over the world.$B$BIt\'s certainly faster than running everywhere. Though, I won\'t stop you if that is your preference.', 0),
(97257, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'You have done well to come this far. You do the Windshapers honor, $N.', 0),
(97284, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How goes the slaughter?', 0),
(97332, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Can\'t you see I\'m busy?', 0),
(97378, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you defeated Mirrorscale, $N?$B$BBe warned, it is said her belly scales are so luminous that they cause her prey to falter momentarily giving her an opportunity to attack.', 0),
(97490, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I should\'ve paid for a bigger lot.', 0),
(97617, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Well?', 0),
(97884, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ah, you have returned. Were you successful in recovering my family\'s tome? What state is Sunnyglade in?$B$BThe last time I laid eyes on my old town, it was being burnt to ash.$B$BI joined the Stormwind army and traveled all the way up here to Lordaeron and died in the second war, so I never had a chance to return. I heard of efforts to rebuild Sunnyglade but I am not sure they ever were able to.', 0),
(97918, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I can teach you once you\'ve gained some skill with your profession.', 0),
(97950, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Come talk to me again once you\'ve gained some skill with your profession.', 0),
(97954, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Come talk to me again once you\'ve gained some skill with your profession.', 0),
(97963, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yes, I can teach you.', 0),
(98071, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Lookin\' ta try a new ale?', 0),
(98192, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Krak need more hide from bities. It good you help.', 0),
(98208, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Have you been to the wreckage? It is a most somber sight.', 0),
(98233, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Blast! I wish my friends hadn\'t goaded me into this. They told me that there was no way I could take on one of those wretched oozes by myself. Naturally in my...$B$B<Jameson clears his throat.>$B$B... completely sober state, I thought it was a good idea to prove them wrong.$B$BClearly it didn\'t go the way I had envisioned. That will teach me to try to fight and indulge in the same evening.', 0),
(98246, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'The Razormaw won\'t be none too happy about you taking their eggs, so be ready for a squabble.', 0),
(98284, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Yes, I can teach you.', 0),
(98325, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Are you here to fight? To do what must be done in the name of our Warchief?', 0),
(98477, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'This disturbance of magic has the elders of the Earthen Ring very concerned. Who knows what else could be affected? Time? Reality? Our understanding of these forces is poor. These motes appear to be drawn to powerful practitioners of magic, and are certainly related to this change. It\'s our hope that we can learn more from them.$B$BAny help you provide will earn you the gratitude and esteem of the Earthen Ring.', 0),
(98576, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Ya come to Mai\'ah ready to learn. Dat be good. Ya got da power to touch da strands of da cosmos, but ya also got da wisdom to know dat you need guidance. I can teach ya da first steps to wield dat power.', 0),
(98903, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'How goes the battle for the Darkspear Islands? Have you claimed victory yet?', 0),
(99193, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'Our mages have been captivated studying the properties of this \'Mageweave\' cloth that is so common here on Azeroth. If you could produce a donation of sixty pieces of mageweave cloth it would be a most welcome boon to our studies. Such generosity would surely be noted by the High Order, as well!$B$BIf you have the sixty pieces of mageweave cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I\'m able to take them from you now.', 0),
(99194, 0, 0, 0, 0, '$N, thank you for your previous contributions to the High Order. As we work hard to keep up with our people\'s demand for cloth, runecloth is in particularly short supply. We sincerely hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past!$B$BIf you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. We\'ll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we\'ll go from there.', 0),
(99199, 0, 0, 0, 0, '$N, thank you for your previous contributions to the Windshapers. As we work hard to keep up with our needs for cloth, runecloth is in particularly high demand. We sincerely hope that you will be able to help us as you have in the past!$B$BIf you are willing, please bring me what runecloth you can spare. We\'ll initially accept a single donation of sixty, and then we\'ll go from there.', 0),
(99257, 0, 0, 0, 0, 'I assure you I am not looking to sabotage one of our only means of defense. If a protector does not look as lively and well-nourished as those in our temple, then they are on the last hundred years or so of their lifecycle. If anything, it is a mercy killing.', 0);
